Bundled national legal MCP connectors (desktop installer)
---------------------------------------------------------

The desktop installer additionally bundles thirteen national legal MCP
connectors, each in a separate repository under the Apache License 2.0
(distinct from the MIT connectors above; Apache-2.0 is compatible with
AGPL-3.0 for distribution). Which ones are enabled by default depends on
the installer edition:

  - EU: de-eli-mcp, at-eli-mcp, es-eli-mcp, fi-eli-mcp, ie-eli-mcp,
    nl-eli-mcp, se-eli-mcp, fr-eli-mcp, lu-eli-mcp, it-eli-mcp
  - outside the EU: br-eli-mcp (Brazil), gb-eli-mcp (United Kingdom),
    us-eli-mcp (United States)
  - Copyright (c) 2026 MateMatic Solutions / Wiesław Mazur
  - Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  - https://github.com/matematicsolutions/<name>-eli-mcp

These connectors are Python (fastmcp) and are run from a bundled CPython
runtime (see below). See governance/adr/0136-bundled-python-runtime-eli.md.


Bundled OCR engine (desktop installer)
--------------------------------------

To read scanned files offline, the desktop installer bundles Tesseract OCR
with its Windows build dependencies and two language data files:

  - Tesseract OCR 5.4.0 - Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract
    The Apache-2.0 text and the Tesseract AUTHORS file ship with the installer,
    at `resources/backend/ocr/tesseract/doc/` in an installed Patron.
  - Language data: pol.traineddata, osd.traineddata, from
    https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata (Apache License 2.0 upstream).
  - Statically linked into that Windows build, as reported by
    `tesseract --version`: Leptonica 1.84.1 (own two-clause BSD-style license,
    http://www.leptonica.org), libjpeg-turbo 3.0.1, libpng 1.6.43, libtiff 4.6.0,
    zlib 1.3, libwebp 1.4.0, libgif 5.2.1, OpenJPEG 2.5.2 - all permissive
    (BSD / zlib / libpng / IJG family).

    Their notices ship as `resources/backend/ocr/THIRD-PARTY-OCR-LICENSES.txt`,
    with Leptonica's copyright notice reproduced in full as its clause 2 requires
    for a binary distribution. The 1.1.0 installers carried only Tesseract's own
    Apache-2.0 text; the file was added on 2026-08-18 after that gap was measured,
    and the build now fails if it is missing.

The OCR engine is selected by configuration (`PATRON_OCR_CMD`), so Patron can
also run against a different local engine; only Tesseract is redistributed here.


Bundled embedding model (desktop installer)
-------------------------------------------

Semantic retrieval runs locally, so the installer bundles an ONNX embedding
model instead of calling an embedding API:

  - Xenova/multilingual-e5-small - ONNX conversion for Transformers.js
    https://huggingface.co/Xenova/multilingual-e5-small
  - Converted from intfloat/multilingual-e5-small, licensed MIT
    https://huggingface.co/intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
  - The conversion carries no separate license of its own; MIT applies.

Without the model Patron still starts and retrieval degrades to BM25 plus the
citation graph (ADR-0071 - fail-closed, no download at first run).


Bundled CPython runtime (desktop installer)
-------------------------------------------

To run the Python EU connectors offline without requiring a system Python,
the desktop installer bundles a standalone CPython build:

  - CPython - Python Software Foundation License v2
    https://www.python.org (via python-build-standalone, astral-sh/uv)
  - python-build-standalone - https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone

Python packages installed into the bundled runtime (resolved at build time):
  - fastmcp (Apache-2.0), mcp (MIT), httpx (BSD-3-Clause),
    pydantic (MIT), anyio (MIT), diskcache (Apache-2.0),
    uvicorn/starlette and transitive dependencies (BSD/MIT/Apache-2.0).
  Their full licenses can be inspected via
  `py-runtime/python.exe -m pip show <package>` or in each package's
  site-packages dist-info.
